{"profiles":[{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"pufflegs","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Drab Pufflegs","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Haplophaedia Pufflegs","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Haplophaedia","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Haplophaedia Simon, 1918","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2476335},"ottId":192751,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Haplophaedia","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Haplophaedia is a small genus of hummingbirds, which – together with the members of the genus Eriocnemis – are known as pufflegs. They are found at low levels in humid forest, woodland and shrub at altitudes of 1,200 to 3,100 m (3,900 to 10,200 ft) in the Andes of Bolivia, Peru, Ecuador, and Colombia.","revisionId":1289848485,"title":"Haplophaedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haplophaedia","wikidataId":"Q1033762"}},{"commonNames":[],"ottId":211119,"scientificName":"Buceros","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Buceros, from Ancient Greek βοῦς (boûs), meaning \"ox\", and κέρας (kéras), meaning \"horn\", is a genus of large Asian hornbills (family Bucerotidae).","revisionId":1374250507,"title":"Buceros","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buceros","wikidataId":"Q850627"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Tyrant manakins","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Small Tyrant-Manakins","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Tyranneutes","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Tyranneutes P.L.Sclater & Salvin, 1881","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2487707},"ottId":232047,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Tyranneutes","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Tyranneutes is a genus of South American birds in the family Pipridae. Both sexes somewhat resemble females of other manakins, but are even smaller.","revisionId":1318670382,"title":"Tyranneutes","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyranneutes","wikidataId":"Q1059789"}},{"comm